00:25:39.130 --> 00:25:41.380
I think one of the things
that I found really powerful

00:25:41.380 --> 00:25:44.130
about the fix for action
thing in the spring

00:25:44.130 --> 00:25:46.257
was that we did have
the full audience.

00:25:46.257 --> 00:25:48.090
I think one of the
things that I was talking

00:25:48.090 --> 00:25:49.980
about with a student
in our breakout group

00:25:49.980 --> 00:25:54.050
was you lose that energy in
Zoom between the performer

00:25:54.050 --> 00:25:55.050
and the audience member.

00:25:55.050 --> 00:25:56.880
And I think that really
affects performers,

00:25:56.880 --> 00:25:58.230
and I think as an
audience member we

00:25:58.230 --> 00:25:59.610
just kind of check
out more easily

00:25:59.610 --> 00:26:01.290
because we're used
to being a little bit

00:26:01.290 --> 00:26:03.300
visible in an audience space.

00:26:03.300 --> 00:26:04.680
If you fall asleep
you eventually

00:26:04.680 --> 00:26:06.520
feel embarrassed, usually.

00:26:06.520 --> 00:26:09.570
There's a bit more
responsibility to the moment

00:26:09.570 --> 00:26:11.820
and what I really loved about
the end of that section,

00:26:11.820 --> 00:26:14.430
especially when there was
so much community discussion

00:26:14.430 --> 00:26:17.700
and engagement with the song and
the spirit of the whole thing,

00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:21.060
is that we did have
everybody on camera.

00:26:21.060 --> 00:26:23.110
I mean most people were
on camera the whole time.

00:26:23.110 --> 00:26:25.777
And it was really powerful to be
able to scroll through and just

00:26:25.777 --> 00:26:27.950
see people experiencing the
same thing that you were

00:26:27.950 --> 00:26:30.450
and I recall hearing from the
artists involved in that piece

00:26:30.450 --> 00:26:32.610
as well that it made a
difference to see people

00:26:32.610 --> 00:26:35.400
watching you as
opposed to just looking

00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:37.860
at your own self in the
camera the whole time.

00:26:37.860 --> 00:26:41.137
And I think those things
were really powerful

00:26:41.137 --> 00:26:42.220
and made a big difference.

00:26:42.220 --> 00:26:45.542
It was a small thing that
I think had a huge impact.

00:26:45.542 --> 00:26:47.250
We spent so much time
thinking about what

00:26:47.250 --> 00:26:48.930
would engage our
audience, but it's also

00:26:48.930 --> 00:26:52.500
important to engage the speakers
and the performers as well.

00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:56.730
And like Susan said, the
quality of the performance

00:26:56.730 --> 00:27:02.480
goes way up when people feel
that pressure and that support.

